        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Paiute',
            subtitle: 'Hawaiian Draw and Discard',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Paiute is a Hawaiian draw-and-discard game similar to Knock Poker. Players draw and discard to form five- or six-card poker combinations. A turn-up card sets the wild rank. Unique: a player can call with a six-card hand (Three Pairs, called Paiute) on their first draw only.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Hawaiian game; documented from contributions by Derek Bal, Malia Pugh, and Pomai T.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two to five players use a standard international 52-card pack; ace ranks high. Five cards are dealt to each player; the next card is turned face up to set the wild rank for that deal.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card pack. Ace ranks high.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck, chips or money for stakes.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Five cards to each player. Next card turned face up becomes the wild card (e.g. 3 â†’ all 3s wild). Remainder stacked face down with wild card partly visible = stock.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Joker Wild: Use Jokers as wild cards instead of a turn-up card.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Opposite Colour Wild: Only same rank, opposite colour to turn-up are wild (e.g. 5â™  turn-up â†’ 5â™¥ 5â™¦ wild).',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Royal Beats Five: Royal Flush ranks above Five of a Kind.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Six-Player Paiute: With 6+ players, Paiute (Three Pairs) can be called at any time, not only first round.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
